('110336', 'entity', 'SHAHID KARRAZI INDUSTRIES', 'SHAHID KARRAZI INDUSTRIES', 'Iran', 'IRe.068', '2010-06-09', NULL, 'Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'Owned or controlled by, or acts on behalf of, SBIG. [Old Reference # E.29.I.17]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110335', 'entity', 'SHAHID SATTARI INDUSTRIES', 'SHAHID SATTARI INDUSTRIES', 'Iran', 'IRe.069', '2010-06-09', NULL, 'Southeast Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'Owned or controlled by, or acts on behalf of, SBIG. [Old Reference # E.29.I.18]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110334', 'entity', 'SHAHID SAYYADE SHIRAZI INDUSTRIES (SSSI)', 'SHAHID SAYYADE SHIRAZI INDUSTRIES SSSI', 'Iran', 'IRe.070', '2010-06-09', NULL, 'Next To Nirou Battery Mfg. Co, Shahid Babaii Expressway, Nobonyad Square, Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of); Pasdaran St., P.O. Box 16765, Tehran, 1835, Iran (Islamic Republic of); Babaei Highway - Next to Niru M.F.G, Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'SSSI is owned or controlled by, or acts on behalf of, DIO. [Old Reference # E.29.I.19]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110333', 'entity', 'SHO''A'' AVIATION', 'SHO A AVIATION', 'Iran', 'IRe.071', '2007-03-24', NULL, NULL, 'Produces micro-lights which IRGC has claimed it is using as part of its asymmetric warfare doctrine. [Old Reference # E.47.B.3]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110332', 'entity', 'SOUTH SHIPPING LINE IRAN (SSL)', 'SOUTH SHIPPING LINE IRAN SSL', 'Iran', 'IRe.072', '2010-06-09', NULL, 'Qaem Magham Farahani St., Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of); Apt. No. 7, 3rd Floor, No. 2, 4th Alley, Gandi Ave., Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', '[Old Reference # E.29.III.3]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110331', 'entity', 'SPECIAL INDUSTRIES GROUP (SIG)', 'SPECIAL INDUSTRIES GROUP SIG', 'Iran', 'IRe.073', '2010-06-09', NULL, 'Pasdaran Avenue, PO Box 19585/777, Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'Subordinate of DIO. [Old Reference # E.29.I.20]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110330', 'entity', 'TAMAS COMPANY', 'TAMAS', 'Iran', 'IRe.074', '2008-03-03', NULL, NULL, 'Involved in enrichment-related activities. TAMAS is the overarching body, under which four subsidiaries have been established, including one for uranium extraction to concentration and another in charge of uranium processing, enrichment and waste. [Old Reference # E.03.III.12]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110329', 'entity', 'TIZ PARS', 'TIZ PARS', 'Iran', 'IRe.075', '2010-06-09', NULL, 'Damavand Tehran Highway, Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'Tiz Pars is a cover name for SHIG. Between April and July 2007, Tiz Pars attempted to procure a five axis laser welding and cutting machine, which could make a material contribution to Iran''s missile programme, on behalf of SHIG. [Old Reference # E.29.I.21]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110328', 'entity', 'YA MAHDI INDUSTRIES GROUP', 'A MAHDI INDUSTRIES', 'Iran', 'IRe.076', '2007-03-24', NULL, NULL, 'Subordinate to AIO, which is involved in international purchases of missile equipment. [Old Reference # E.47.A.10]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110327', 'entity', 'YAS AIR', 'YAS AIR', 'Iran', 'IRe.077', '2012-12-20', NULL, 'Mehrabad International Airport, Next to Terminal No. 6, Tehran, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'Yas Air is the new name for Pars Air, a company that was owned by Pars Aviation Services Company, which in turn was designated by the United Nations Security Council in resolution 1747 (2007). Yas Air has assisted Pars Aviation Services Company, a United Nations-designated entity, in violating paragraph 5 of resolution 1747 (2007). [Old Reference # I.AC.50.20.12.12.(1)]', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('110326', 'entity', 'YAZD METALLURGY INDUSTRIES (YMI)', 'YAZD METALLURGY INDUSTRIES YMI', 'Iran', 'IRe.078', '2010-06-09', NULL, 'Pasdaran Avenue, next to Telecommunication Industry, Tehran, 16588, Iran (Islamic Republic of); Postal Box 89195/878, Yazd, Iran (Islamic Republic of); P.O. Box 89195-678, Yazd, Iran (Islamic Republic of); Km 5 of Taft Road, Yazd, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'YMI is a subordinate of DIO. [Old Reference #E.29.I.22].', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690735', 'entity', 'KOREA MINING DEVELOPMENT TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREA MINING DEVELOPMENT TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.001', '2009-04-24', NULL, 'Central District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Primary arms dealer and main exporter of goods and equipment related to ballistic missiles and conventional weapons.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690751', 'entity', 'KOREA RYONBONG GENERAL CORPORATION', 'KOREA RYONBONG GENERAL', 'DPRK', 'KPe.002', '2009-04-24', NULL, 'Pot’onggang District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Rakwon-dong, Pothonggang District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Defense conglomerate specializing in acquisition for DPRK defense industries and support to that country’s military-related sales.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690752', 'entity', 'TANCHON COMMERCIAL BANK', 'TANCHON COMMERCIAL BANK', 'DPRK', 'KPe.003', '2009-04-24', NULL, 'Saemul 1-Dong Pyongchon District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Main DPRK financial entity for sales of conventional arms, ballistic missiles, and goods related to the assembly and manufacture of such weapons.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690753', 'entity', 'NAMCHONGANG TRADING CORPORATION', 'NAMCHONGANG TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.004', '2009-07-16', NULL, 'Chilgol, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Sengujadong 11-2/(or Kwangbok-dong), Mangyongdae District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Namchongang is a DPRK trading company subordinate to the General Bureau of Atomic Energy (GBAE). Namchongang has been involved in the procurement of Japanese origin vacuum pumps that were identified at a DPRK nuclear facility, as well as nuclear-related procurement associated with a German individual. It has further been involved in the purchase of aluminum tubes and other equipment specifically suitable for a uranium enrichment program from the late 1990s. Its representative is a former diplomat who served as DPRK’s representative for the IAEA inspection of the Yongbyon nuclear facilities in 2007. Namchongang''s proliferation activities are of grave concern given the DPRK’s past proliferation activities. Telephone numbers: +850-2-18111, 18222 (ext. 8573). Facsimile number: +850-2-381-4687.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690755', 'entity', 'HONG KONG ELECTRONICS', 'HONG KONG ELECTRONICS', 'DPRK', 'KPe.005', '2009-07-16', NULL, 'Sanaee Street, Kish Island, Iran (Islamic Republic of)', 'Owned or controlled by, or acts or purports to act for or on behalf of Tanchon Commercial Bank and KOMID. Hong Kong Electronics has transferred millions of dollars of proliferation-related funds on behalf of Tanchon Commercial Bank and KOMID (both designated by the Committee in April 2009) since 2007. Hong Kong Electronics has facilitated the movement of money from Iran to the DPRK on behalf of KOMID.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690756', 'entity', 'KOREA HYOKSIN TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREA HYOKSIN TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.006', '2009-07-16', NULL, 'Rakwon-dong, Pothonggang District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'A DPRK company based in Pyongyang that is subordinate to Korea Ryonbong General Corporation (designated by the Committee in April 2009) and is involved in the development of WMD.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690758', 'entity', 'GENERAL BUREAU OF ATOMIC ENERGY (GBAE)', 'GENERAL BUREAU OF ATOMIC ENERGY GBAE', 'DPRK', 'KPe.007', '2009-07-16', NULL, 'Haeudong, Pyongchen District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The GBAE is responsible for the DPRK’s nuclear program, which includes the Yongbyon Nuclear Research Center and its 5 MWe (25 MWt) plutonium production research reactor, as well as its fuel fabrication and reprocessing facilities. The GBAE has held nuclear-related meetings and discussions with the International Atomic Energy Agency. GBAE is the primary DPRK government agency that oversees nuclear programs, including the operation of the Yongbyon Nuclear Research Center. Changed name as Ministry of Atomic Energy Industry (KPe.027) in 2013.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22')
ON CONFLICT(uid) DO UPDATE SET entity_type = excluded.entity_type, primary_name = excluded.primary_name, name_normalized = excluded.name_normalized, un_list_type = excluded.un_list_type, reference_number = excluded.reference_number, listed_on = excluded.listed_on, nationality = excluded.nationality, addresses = excluded.addresses, remarks = excluded.remarks, source_url = excluded.source_url, last_updated = excluded.last_updated WHERE un_sanctions_entries.entity_type IS NOT excluded.entity_type OR un_sanctions_entries.primary_name IS NOT excluded.primary_name OR un_sanctions_entries.name_normalized IS NOT excluded.name_normalized OR un_sanctions_entries.un_list_type IS NOT excluded.un_list_type OR un_sanctions_entries.reference_number IS NOT excluded.reference_number OR un_sanctions_entries.listed_on IS NOT excluded.listed_on OR un_sanctions_entries.nationality IS NOT excluded.nationality OR un_sanctions_entries.addresses IS NOT excluded.addresses OR un_sanctions_entries.remarks IS NOT excluded.remarks OR un_sanctions_entries.source_url IS NOT excluded.source_url;
INSERT INTO un_sanctions_entries (uid, entity_type, primary_name, name_normalized, un_list_type, reference_number, listed_on, nationality, addresses, remarks, source_url, source_tier, last_updated) VALUES
('690759', 'entity', 'KOREAN TANGUN TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREAN TANGUN TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.008', '2009-07-16', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Tangun Trading Corporation is subordinate to DPRK’s Second Academy of Natural Sciences and is primarily responsible for the procurement of commodities and technologies to support DPRK’s defense research and development programs, including, but not limited to, WMD and delivery system programs and procurement, including materials that are controlled or prohibited under relevant multilateral control regimes.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690760', 'entity', 'AMROGGANG DEVELOPMENT BANKING CORPORATION', 'AMROGGANG DEVELOPMENT BANKING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.009', '2012-05-02', NULL, 'Tongan-dong, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Amroggang, which was established in 2006, is a Tanchon Commercial Bank-related company managed by Tanchon officials. Tanchon plays a role in financing KOMID’s sales of ballistic missiles and has also been involved in ballistic missile transactions from KOMID to Iran’s Shahid Hemmat Industrial Group (SHIG). Tanchon Commercial Bank was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is the main DPRK financial entity for sales of conventional arms, ballistic missiles, and goods related to the assembly and manufacture of such weapons. KOMID was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is the DPRK’s primary arms dealer and main exporter of goods and equipment related to ballistic missiles and conventional weapons. The Security Council designated SHIG in resolution 1737 (2006) as an entity involved in Iran’s ballistic missile programme.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690761', 'entity', 'GREEN PINE ASSOCIATED CORPORATION', 'GREEN PINE ASSOCIATED', 'DPRK', 'KPe.010', '2012-05-02', NULL, 'c/o Reconnaissance General Bureau Headquarters, Hyongjesan-Guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Nungrado, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Rakrang No. 1 Rakrang District Pyongyang Korea, Chilgol-1 dong, Mangyongdae District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Green Pine Associated Corporation (“Green Pine”) has taken over many of the activities of the Korea Mining Development Trading Corporation (KOMID). KOMID was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is the DPRK''s primary arms dealer and main exporter of goods and equipment related to ballistic missiles and conventional weapons. Green Pine is also responsible for approximately half of the arms and related materiel exported by the DPRK. Green Pine has been identified for sanctions for exporting arms or related material from North Korea. Green Pine specializes in the production of maritime military craft and armaments, such as submarines, military boats and missile systems, and has exported torpedoes and technical assistance to Iranian defence-related firms. Telephone number: +850-2-18111(ext. 8327). Facsimile number: +850-2-3814685 and +850-2-3813372. Email addresses: pac@silibank.com and kndic@co.chesin.com.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690762', 'entity', 'KOREA HEUNGJIN TRADING COMPANY', 'KOREA HEUNGJIN TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.011', '2012-05-02', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Korea Heungjin Trading Company is used by KOMID for trading purposes. We suspect it has been involved in supplying missile-related goods to Iran’s Shahid Hemmat Industrial Group (SHIG). Heungjin has been associated with KOMID, and, more specifically, KOMID’s procurement office. Heungjin has been used to procure an advanced digital controller with applications in missile design. KOMID was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is the DPRK’s primary arms dealer and main exporter of goods and equipment related to ballistic missiles and conventional weapons. The Security Council designated SHIG in resolution 1737 (2006) as an entity involved in Iran’s ballistic missile programme.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690763', 'entity', 'KOREAN COMMITTEE FOR SPACE TECHNOLOGY', 'KOREAN COMMITTEE FOR SPACE TECHNOLOGY', 'DPRK', 'KPe.012', '2013-01-22', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Korean Committee for Space Technology (KCST) orchestrated the DPRK’s launches on 13 April 2012 and 12 December 2012 via the satellite control center and Sohae launch area.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690764', 'entity', 'BANK OF EAST LAND', 'BANK OF EAST LAND', 'DPRK', 'KPe.013', '2013-01-22', NULL, 'PO Box 32, BEL Building, Jonseung-Dung, Moranbong District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'DPRK financial institution Bank of East Land facilitates weapons-related transactions for, and other support to, arms manufacturer and exporter Green Pine Associated Corporation (Green Pine). Bank of East Land has actively worked with Green Pine to transfer funds in a manner that circumvents sanctions. In 2007 and 2008, Bank of East Land facilitated transactions involving Green Pine and Iranian financial institutions, including Bank Melli and Bank Sepah. The Security Council designated Bank Sepah in resolution 1747 (2007) for providing support to Iran’s ballistic missile program. Green Pine was designated by the Committee in April 2012.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690765', 'entity', 'KOREA KUMRYONG TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREA KUMRYONG TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.014', '2013-01-22', NULL, NULL, 'Used as an alias by the Korea Mining Development Trading Corporation (KOMID) to carry out procurement activities. KOMID was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is the DPRK’s primary arms dealer and main exporter of goods and equipment related to ballistic missiles and conventional weapons.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690766', 'entity', 'TOSONG TECHNOLOGY TRADING CORPORATION', 'TOSONG TECHNOLOGY TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.015', '2013-01-22', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Korea Mining Development Corporation (KOMID) is the parent company of Tosong Technology Trading Corporation. KOMID was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is the DPRK’s primary arms dealer and main exporter of goods and equipment related to ballistic missiles and conventional weapons.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690767', 'entity', 'KOREA RYONHA MACHINERY JOINT VENTURE CORPORATION', 'KOREA RYONHA MACHINERY JOINT VENTURE', 'DPRK', 'KPe.016', '2013-01-22', NULL, 'Tongan-dong, Central District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Mangungdae-gu, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Mangyongdae District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Ryonbong General Corporation is the parent company of Korea Ryonha Machinery Joint Venture Corporation. Korea Ryonbong General Corporation was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is a defense conglomerate specializing in acquisition for DPRK defense industries and support to that country''s military-related sales. Email addresses: ryonha@silibank.com; sjc-117@hotmail.com; and millim@silibank.com. Telephone numbers: 850-2-18111; 850-2-18111-8642; and 850 2 18111-3818642. Facsimile number: 850-2-381-4410', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690768', 'entity', 'LEADER (HONG KONG) INTERNATIONAL', 'LEADER HONG KONG', 'DPRK', 'KPe.017', '2013-01-22', NULL, 'LM-873, RM B, 14/F, Wah Hen Commercial Centre, 383 Hennessy Road, Wanchai, China, Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, China, Hong Kong Special Administrative Region', 'Facilitates shipments on behalf of the Korea Mining Development Trading Corporation (KOMID). KOMID was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is the DPRK’s primary arms dealer and main exporter of goods and equipment related to ballistic missiles and conventional weapons. Hong Kong company registration number 1177053.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690769', 'entity', 'SECOND ACADEMY OF NATURAL SCIENCES', 'SECOND ACADEMY OF NATURAL SCIENCES', 'DPRK', 'KPe.018', '2013-03-07', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Second Academy of Natural Sciences is a national-level organization responsible for research and development of the DPRK’s advanced weapons systems, including missiles and probably nuclear weapons. The Second Academy of Natural Sciences uses a number of subordinate organizations to obtain technology, equipment, and information from overseas, including Tangun Trading Corporation, for use in the DPRK’s missile and probably nuclear weapons programs. Tangun Trading Corporation was designated by the Committee in July 2009 and is primarily responsible for the procurement of commodities and technologies to support DPRK’s defense research and development programs, including, but not limited to, weapons of mass destruction and delivery system programs and procurement, including materials that are controlled or prohibited under relevant multilateral control regimes.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690770', 'entity', 'KOREA COMPLEX EQUIPMENT IMPORT CORPORATION', 'KOREA COMPLEX EQUIPMENT IMPORT', 'DPRK', 'KPe.019', '2013-03-07', NULL, 'Rakwon-dong, Pothonggang District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Ryonbong General Corporation is the parent company of Korea Complex Equipment Import Corporation. Korea Ryonbong General Corporation was designated by the Committee in April 2009 and is a defense conglomerate specializing in acquisition for DPRK defense industries and support to that country’s military-related sales.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908046', 'entity', 'OCEAN MARITIME MANAGEMENT COMPANY, LIMITED (OMM)', 'OCEAN MARITIME MANAGEMENT COMPANY LIMITED OMM', 'DPRK', 'KPe.020', '2014-07-28', NULL, 'Donghung Dong, Central District, PO Box 120, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Dongheung-dong Changgwang Street, Chung-Ku, PO Box 125, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Ocean Maritime Management Company, Limited is the operator/manager of the vessel Chong Chon Gang. It played a key role in arranging the shipment of concealed cargo of arms and related materiel from Cuba to the DPRK in July 2013. As such, Ocean Maritime Management Company, Limited contributed to activities prohibited by the resolutions, namely the arms embargo imposed by resolution 1718 (2006), as modified by resolution 1874 (2009), and contributed to the evasion of the measures imposed by these resolutions. International Maritime Organization (IMO) Number: 1790183.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908510', 'entity', 'ACADEMY OF NATIONAL DEFENSE SCIENCE', 'ACADEMY OF NATIONAL DEFENSE SCIENCE', 'DPRK', 'KPe.021', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Academy of National Defense Science is involved in the DPRK''s efforts to advance the development of its ballistic missile and nuclear weapons programs.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908516', 'entity', 'CHONGCHONGANG SHIPPING COMPANY', 'CHONGCHONGANG SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.022', '2016-03-02', NULL, '817 Haeun, Donghung-dong, Central District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; 817, Haeum, Tonghun-dong, Chung-gu, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'IMO Number: 5342883. The Chongchongang Shipping Company, through its vessel, the Chong Chon Gang, attempted to directly import the illicit shipment of conventional weapons and arms to the DPRK in July 2013.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908499', 'entity', 'DAEDONG CREDIT BANK (DCB)', 'DAEDONG CREDIT BANK DCB', 'DPRK', 'KPe.023', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Suite 401, Potonggang Hotel, Ansan-Dong, Pyongchon District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Ansan-dong, Botonggang Hotel, Pongchon, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'SWIFT: DCBKKPPY. Daedong Credit Bank has provided financial services to the Korea Mining Development Trading Corporation (KOMID) and Tanchon Commercial Bank. Since at least 2007, DCB has facilitated hundreds of financial transactions worth millions of dollars on behalf of KOMID and Tanchon Commercial Bank. In some cases, DCB has knowingly facilitated transactions by using deceptive financial practices.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908517', 'entity', 'HESONG TRADING COMPANY', 'HESONG TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.024', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Korea Mining Development Trading Corporation (KOMID) is the parent company of Hesong Trading Corporation.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908518', 'entity', 'KOREA KWANGSON BANKING CORPORATION (KKBC)', 'KOREA KWANGSON BANKING CORPORATION KKBC', 'DPRK', 'KPe.025', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Jungson-dong, Sungri Street, Central District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'KKBC provides financial services in support to Tanchon Commercial Bank and Korea Hyoksin Trading Corporation, a subordinate of the Korea Ryonbong General Corporation. Tanchon Commercial Bank has used KKBC to facilitate funds transfers likely amounting to millions of dollars, including transfers involving Korea Mining Development Corporation related funds.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908519', 'entity', 'KOREA KWANGSONG TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREA KWANGSONG TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.026', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Rakwon-dong, Pothonggang District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Korea Ryongbong General Corporation is the parent company of Korea Kwangsong Trading Corporation.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908520', 'entity', 'MINISTRY OF ATOMIC ENERGY INDUSTRY', 'MINISTRY OF ATOMIC ENERGY INDUSTRY', 'DPRK', 'KPe.027', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Haeun-2-dong, Pyongchon District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Ministry of Atomic Energy Industry was created in 2013 for the purpose of modernizing the DPRK’s atomic energy industry to increase the production of nuclear materials, improve their quality, and further develop an independent DPRK nuclear industry. As such, the MAEI is known to be a critical player in the DPRK’s development of nuclear weapons and is in charge of day-to-day operation of the country’s nuclear weapons program, and under it are other nuclear-related organizations. Under this ministry are a number of nuclear-related organizations and research centers, as well as two committees: an Isotope Application Committee and a Nuclear Energy Committee. The MAEI also directs a nuclear research center at Yongbyun, the site of the DPRK''s known plutonium facilities. Furthermore, in the 2015 Panel of Experts (POE) report, the POE stated that Ri Je-son, a former director of the GBAE who was designated by the Committee established pursuant to resolution 1718 (2006) in 2009 for engagement in or support for nuclear related programs, was appointed as head of the MAEI on April 9, 2014.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908522', 'entity', 'MUNITIONS INDUSTRY DEPARTMENT', 'MUNITIONS INDUSTRY DEPARTMENT', 'DPRK', 'KPe.028', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Munitions Industry Department is involved in key aspects of the DPRK''s missile program. MID is responsible for overseeing the development of the DPRK''s ballistic missiles, including the Taepo Dong-2.The MID oversees the DPRK''s weapons production and R&D programs, including the DPRK''s ballistic missile program. The Second Economic Committee and the Second Academy of Natural Sciences – also designated in August 2010 – are subordinate to the MID. The MID in recent years has worked to develop the KN08 road-mobile ICBM. The MID oversees the DPRK’s nuclear program. The Nuclear Weapons Institute is subordinate to the MID.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908523', 'entity', 'NATIONAL AEROSPACE TECHNOLOGY ADMINISTRATION', 'NATIONAL AEROSPACE TECHNOLOGY ADMINISTRATION', 'DPRK', 'KPe.029', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'NATA is involved in the DPRK''s development of space science and technology, including satellite launches and carrier rockets.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908524', 'entity', 'OFFICE 39', 'OFFICE 39', 'DPRK', 'KPe.030', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Second KWP Government Building (Korean – Ch’o’ngsa, Urban Town (Korean-Dong), Chung Ward, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Chung-Guyok (Central District), Sosong Street, Kyongrim-Dong, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Changwang Street, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'DPRK government entity', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908526', 'entity', 'RECONNAISSANCE GENERAL BUREAU', 'RECONNAISSANCE GENERAL BUREAU', 'DPRK', 'KPe.031', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Hyongjesan-Guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Nungrado, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Reconnaissance General Bureau is the DPRK''s premiere intelligence organization, created in early 2009 by the merger of existing intelligence organizations from the Korean Workers'' Party, the Operations Department and Office 35, and the Reconnaissance Bureau of the Korean People''s Army. The Reconnaissance General Bureau trades in conventional arms and controls the DPRK conventional arms firm Green Pine Associated Corporation.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908528', 'entity', 'SECOND ECONOMIC COMMITTEE', 'SECOND ECONOMIC COMMITTEE', 'DPRK', 'KPe.032', '2016-03-02', NULL, 'Kangdong, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Second Economic Committee is involved in key aspects of the DPRK''s missile program. The Second Economic Committee is responsible for overseeing the production of the DPRK''s ballistic missiles, and directs the activities of KOMID.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908563', 'entity', 'KOREA UNITED DEVELOPMENT BANK', 'KOREA UNITED DEVELOPMENT BANK', 'DPRK', 'KPe.033', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea United Development Bank operates in the financial services industry of the DPRK economy. SWIFT/BIC: KUDBKPPY', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908551', 'entity', 'ILSIM INTERNATIONAL BANK', 'ILSIM INTERNATIONAL BANK', 'DPRK', 'KPe.034', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Ilsim International Bank is affiliated with the DPRK military and has a close relationship with Korea Kwangson Banking Corporation (KKBC). Ilsim International Bank has attempted to evade United Nations sanctions. SWIFT: ILSIKPPY', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908552', 'entity', 'KOREA DAESONG BANK', 'KOREA DAESONG BANK', 'DPRK', 'KPe.035', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Segori-dong, Gyongheung St. Potonggang District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Daesong Bank is owned and controlled by Office 39 of the Korea Workers’ Party. SWIFT/BIC: KDBKKPPY', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908553', 'entity', 'SINGWANG ECONOMICS AND TRADING GENERAL CORPORATION', 'SINGWANG ECONOMICS AND TRADING GENERAL', 'DPRK', 'KPe.036', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Singwang Economics and Trading General Corporation is a DPRK firm for trading in coal. DPRK generates a significant share of the money for its nuclear and ballistic missile programs by mining natural resources and selling those resources abroad.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908557', 'entity', 'KOREA FOREIGN TECHNICAL TRADE CENTER', 'KOREA FOREIGN TECHNICAL TRADE CENTER', 'DPRK', 'KPe.037', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Foreign Technical Trade Center is a DPRK firm trading in coal. DPRK generates a significant share of the funds needed to finance its nuclear and ballistic missile programs by mining natural resources and selling those resources abroad.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908561', 'entity', 'KOREA PUGANG TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREA PUGANG TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.038', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Rakwon-dong, Pothonggang District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Pugang Trading Corporation is owned by the Korea Ryonbong General Corporation, DPRK’s defense conglomerate specializing in acquisition for DPRK defense industries and support to Pyongyang’s military related sales.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908562', 'entity', 'KOREA INTERNATIONAL CHEMICAL JOINT VENTURE COMPANY', 'KOREA INTERNATIONAL CHEMICAL JOINT VENTURE', 'DPRK', 'KPe.039', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Hamhung, South Hamgyong Province, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Man gyongdae-kuyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Mangyungdae-gu, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea International Chemical Joint Venture Company is a subsidiary of Korea Ryonbong General Corporation – DPRK’s defense conglomerate specializing in acquisition for DPRK defense industries and support to Pyongyang’s military related sales – and has engaged in proliferation-related transactions.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908556', 'entity', 'DCB FINANCE LIMITED', 'DCB FINANCE LIMITED', 'DPRK', 'KPe.040', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Akara Building, 24 de Castro Street, Wickhams Cay I, Road Town, Tortola, British Virgin Islands; Dalian, China', 'DCB Finance Limited is a front company for Daedong Credit Bank (DCB), a listed entity.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908559', 'entity', 'KOREA TAESONG TRADING COMPANY', 'KOREA TAESONG TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.041', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Taesong Trading Company has acted on behalf of KOMID in dealings with Syria.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908560', 'entity', 'KOREA DAESONG GENERAL TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREA DAESONG GENERAL TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.042', '2016-11-30', NULL, 'Pulgan Gori Dong 1, Potonggang District, Pyongyang City, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Daesong General Trading Corporation is affiliated with Office 39 through minerals (gold) exports, metals, machinery, agricultural products, ginseng, jewelry, and light industry products.Telephone: +850-2-18111-8208. Fax: +850-2-381-4432. Email: daesong@star-co.net.kp.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908594', 'entity', 'KANGBONG TRADING CORPORATION', 'KANGBONG TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.043', '2017-06-02', NULL, 'Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Kangbong Trading Corporation sold, supplied, transferred, or purchased, directly or indirectly, to or from the DPRK, metal, graphite, coal, or software, where revenue or goods received may benefit the Government of the DPRK or the Workers’ Party of Korea. The Kangbong Trading Corporation’s parent is the Ministry of People’s Armed Forces', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908595', 'entity', 'KOREA KUMSAN TRADING CORPORATION', 'KOREA KUMSAN TRADING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.044', '2017-06-02', NULL, 'Haeun 2-dong, Pyogchon District, Pyongyang City/Mangyongdae, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Korea Kumsan Trading Corporation is owned or controlled by, or acting or purporting to act for or on behalf of, directly or indirectly, the General Bureau of Atomic Energy, which oversees the DPRK’s nuclear programme. Telephone: +850-2-18111-8550. Fax: +850-2-381-4410/4416. Email: mhs-ip@star-co.net.kp.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908596', 'entity', 'KORYO BANK', 'KORYO BANK', 'DPRK', 'KPe.045', '2017-06-02', NULL, 'Koryo Bank Building, Pulgun Street, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Koryo Bank operates in the financial services industry in the DPRK’s economy and is associated with Office 38 and Office 39 of the KWP', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908597', 'entity', 'STRATEGIC ROCKET FORCE OF THE KOREAN PEOPLE’S ARMY', 'STRATEGIC ROCKET FORCE OF THE KOREAN PEOPLE’S ARMY', 'DPRK', 'KPe.046', '2017-06-02', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Strategic Rocket Force of the Korean People’s Army is in charge of all DPRK ballistic missile programmes and is responsible for SCUD and NODONG launches', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908622', 'entity', 'FOREIGN TRADE BANK (FTB)', 'FOREIGN TRADE BANK FTB', 'DPRK', 'KPe.047', '2017-08-05', NULL, 'FTB Building, Jungsong-dong, Central District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Foreign Trade Bank is a state-owned bank and acts as the DPRK’s primary foreign exchange bank and has provided key financial support to the Korea Kwangson Banking Corporation. SWIFT/BIC: FTBDKPPY.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908623', 'entity', 'KOREAN NATIONAL INSURANCE COMPANY (KNIC)', 'KOREAN NATIONAL INSURANCE COMPANY KNIC', 'DPRK', 'KPe.048', '2017-08-05', NULL, 'Central District, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Korean National Insurance Company is a DPRK financial and insurance company and is affiliated with Office 39.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908624', 'entity', 'KORYO CREDIT DEVELOPMENT BANK', 'KORYO CREDIT DEVELOPMENT BANK', 'DPRK', 'KPe.049', '2017-08-05', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Koryo Credit Development Bank operates in the financial services industry in the DPRK’s economy.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908625', 'entity', 'MANSUDAE OVERSEAS PROJECT GROUP OF COMPANIES', 'MANSUDAE OVERSEAS PROJECT GROUP OF COMPANIES', 'DPRK', 'KPe.050', '2017-08-05', NULL, 'Yanggakdo International Hotel, RYUS, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Mansudae Overseas Project Group of Companies engaged in, facilitated, or was responsible for the exportation of workers from the DPRK to other nations for construction-related activities including for statues and monuments to generate revenue for the Government of the DPRK or the Workers’ Party of Korea. The Mansudae Overseas Project Group of Companies has been reported to conduct business in countries in Africa and Southeast Asia including Angola, Botswana, Benin, Cambodia, Chad, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Equatorial Guinea, Malaysia, Mozambique, Madagascar, Namibia, Syria, Togo, and Zimbabwe.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908627', 'entity', 'CENTRAL MILITARY COMMISSION OF THE WORKERS’ PARTY OF KOREA (CMC)', 'CENTRAL MILITARY COMMISSION OF THE WORKERS’ PARTY OF KOREA CMC', 'DPRK', 'KPe.051', '2017-09-11', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Central Military Commission is responsible for the development and implementation of the Workers’ Party of Korea’s military policies, commands and controls the DPRK’s military, and directs the country’s military defense industries in coordination with the State Affairs Commission.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908628', 'entity', 'ORGANIZATION AND GUIDANCE DEPARTMENT (OGD)', 'ORGANIZATION AND GUIDANCE DEPARTMENT OGD', 'DPRK', 'KPe.052', '2017-09-11', NULL, 'Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Organization and Guidance Department is a very powerful body of the Worker’s Party of Korea. It directs key personnel appointments for the Workers’ Party of Korea, the DPRK’s military, and the DPRK’s government administration. It also purports to control the political affairs of all of the DPRK and is instrumental in implementing the DPRK’s censorship policies.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908629', 'entity', 'PROPAGANDA AND AGITATION DEPARTMENT (PAD)', 'PROPAGANDA AND AGITATION DEPARTMENT PAD', 'DPRK', 'KPe.053', '2017-09-11', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Propaganda and Agitation Department has full control over the media, which it uses as a tool to control the public on behalf of the DPRK leadership. The Propaganda and Agitation Department also engages in or is responsible for censorship by the Government of the DPRK, including newspaper and broadcast censorship.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908657', 'entity', 'MINISTRY OF NATIONAL DEFENCE', 'MINISTRY OF NATIONAL DEFENCE', 'DPRK', 'KPe.054', '2017-12-22', NULL, 'Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'The Ministry of National Defence manages the general administrative and logistical needs of the Korean People’s Army.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908691', 'entity', 'CHANG AN SHIPPING & TECHNOLOGY', 'CHANG AN SHIPPING & TECHNOLOGY', 'DPRK', 'KPe.055', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Room 2105, DL1849, Trend Centre, 29-31 Cheung Lee Street, Chai Wan, Hong Kong, China', 'Registered owner, ship manager, and commercial manager of Panama-flagged vessel HUA FU, a cargo ship that loaded DPRK coal at Najin, DPRK on 24 September 2017.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908670', 'entity', 'CHONMYONG SHIPPING CO', 'CHONMYONG SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.056', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Kalrimgil 2-dong, Mangyongdae-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea; Saemaul 2-dong, Pyongchon-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of CHON MYONG 1, a DPRK-flagged vessel that conducted ship-to-ship transfer of fuel in late December 2017. IMO number: 5571322.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908671', 'entity', 'FIRST OIL JV CO LTD', 'FIRST OIL JV', 'DPRK', 'KPe.057', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Jongbaek 1-dong, Rakrang-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Owner of the DPRK tanker PAEK MA, which was involved in ship-to-ship transfer operations for oil in mid-January 2018. IMO number: 5963351.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908672', 'entity', 'HAPJANGGANG SHIPPING CORP', 'HAPJANGGANG SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.058', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Kumsong 3-dong, Mangyongdae-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of the DPRK tanker NAM SAN 8, believed to have been involved in ship-to-ship transfer operations for oil, and owner of vessel HAP JANG GANG 6. IMO number: 5787684.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908693', 'entity', 'HUAXIN SHIPPING HONGKONG LTD', 'HUAXIN SHIPPING HONGKONG', 'DPRK', 'KPe.059', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Room 2105, Trend Centre, 29-31 Chueng Lee Street, Chai Wan, Hong Kong, China', 'Ship and commercial manager of the ASIA BRIDGE 1. Hong Kong-owned vessel, the probable “ASIA BRIDGE 1” was instructed on 19 October 2017 by Huaxin Shipping to make preparations for entry into Nampo, DPRK to receive a shipment of coal bound for Vietnam. The “ASIA BRIDGE 1” was instructed by an unidentified employee of Huaxin Shipping Ltd. to make preparations to receive 8,000 metric tons of coal and then sail to Cam Pha, Vietnam. The master of the vessel was instructed to cover the ship’s name and other markings using canvas while in port at Nampo.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908673', 'entity', 'KINGLY WON INTERNATIONAL CO., LTD', 'KINGLY WON', 'DPRK', 'KPe.060', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Trust Company Complex, Ajeltake Road, Ajeltake Island, Majuro MH, Marshall Islands', 'In 2017, Tsang Yung Yuan (aka Neil Tsang) and Kingly Won attempted to engage in an oil deal valued at over $1 million with a petroleum company in a third country to illicitly transfer to the DPRK. Kingly Won acted as a broker for that petroleum company and a Chinese company that reached out to Kingly Won to purchase marine oil on its behalf.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908674', 'entity', 'KOREA ACHIM SHIPPING CO', 'KOREA ACHIM SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.061', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Sochang-dong, Chung-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of DPRK tanker CHON MA SAN. DPRK-flagged CHON MA SAN prepared for likely ship-to-ship transfer operations in late January 2018. The master of the DPRK-flagged motor tanker YU JONG 2 reported on 18 November 2017 to an unidentified DPRK-based controller that the vessel was avoiding a storm in advance of a ship-to-ship transfer. The master suggested that the YU JONG 2 load fuel oil before the DPRK-flagged tanker CHON MA SAN since the CHON MA SAN’s larger size was better suited to conduct ship-to-ship transfers in a storm. After the CHON MA SAN loaded fuel oil from a vessel, the YU JONG 2 loaded 1,168 kiloliters of fuel oil on 19 November 2017 through a ship-to-ship transfer operation. IMO number: 5936312.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908675', 'entity', 'KOREA ANSAN SHIPPING COMPANY', 'KOREA ANSAN SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.062', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Pyongchon 1-dong, Pyongchon-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of DPRK tanker AN SAN 1 believed to have been involved in ship-to-ship transfer operations for oil. IMO number: 5676084', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908676', 'entity', 'KOREA MYONGDOK SHIPPING CO', 'KOREA MYONGDOK SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.063', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Chilgol 2-dong, Mangyongdae-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of the YU PHYONG 5. In late November 2017, the YU PHYONG 5 conducted a ship-to-ship transfer of 1,721 metric tons of fuel oil. IMO number: 5985863.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908677', 'entity', 'KOREA SAMJONG SHIPPING', 'KOREA SAMJONG SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.064', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Tonghung-dong, Chung-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of DPRK tankers SAM JONG 1 and SAM JONG 2. Both vessels are believed to have imported refined petroleum to DPRK in violation of UN sanctions in late January 2018. IMO number: 5954061.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908678', 'entity', 'KOREA SAMMA SHIPPING CO', 'KOREA SAMMA SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.065', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Rakrang 3-dong, Rakrang-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'A DPRK-flagged tanker, SAM MA 2 owned by Korea Samma Shipping Company, conducted a ship-to-ship transfer of oil and fabricated documents in mid-October 2017, loading almost 1,600 metric tons of fuel oil in one transaction. The ship master was instructed to erase SAMMA SHIPPING and the Korean words found on the ship’s seal and instead put “Hai Xin You 606” to mask its identity as a DPRK vessel. IMO number: 5145892.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908680', 'entity', 'KOREA YUJONG SHIPPING CO LTD', 'KOREA YUJONG SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.066', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Puksong 2-dong, Pyongchon-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of the DPRK tanker YU JONG 2, which loaded 1,168 kiloliters of fuel oil on 19 November 2017 through a ship-to-ship transfer operation. Company Number IMO 5434358.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908681', 'entity', 'KOTI CORP', 'KOTI', 'DPRK', 'KPe.067', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Panama City, Panama', 'Ship manager and commercial manager of the Panama-flagged vessel KOTI, which conducted ship-to-ship transfers of likely petroleum product to the DPRK-flagged KUM UN SAN 3 on 9 December 2017. IMO number: 5982254.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908967', 'entity', 'MYOHYANG SHIPPING CO', 'MYOHYANG SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.068', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Kumsong 3-dong, Mangyongdae-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Ship manager of DPRK oil products tanker YU SON, which is believed to have been involved in ship-to-ship transfer operations for oil. IMO number: 5988369.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908683', 'entity', 'PAEKMA SHIPPING CO', 'PAEKMA SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.069', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Jongbaek 1-dong, Rakrang-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of the DPRK tanker PAEK MA, which was involved in ship-to-ship transfer operations for oil in mid-January 2018.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908684', 'entity', 'PHYONGCHON SHIPPING & MARINE', 'PHYONGCHON SHIPPING & MARINE', 'DPRK', 'KPe.070', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Otan-dong, Chung-guyok, Pyongyang, Democratic People''s Republic of Korea', 'Registered owner of DPRK tanker JI SONG 6, which is believed to have been involved in ship-to-ship transfer operations of oil in late January 2018. The company also owns vessels JI SONG 8 and WOORY STAR. IMO number: 5878561.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908686', 'entity', 'PRO-GAIN GROUP CORPORATION', 'PRO GAIN', 'DPRK', 'KPe.071', '2018-03-30', NULL, NULL, 'Company owned or controlled by Tsang Yung Yuan and involved in illicit transfers of DPRK coal.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908695', 'entity', 'SHANGHAI DONGFENG SHIPPING CO LTD', 'SHANGHAI DONGFENG SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.072', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Room 601, 433, Chifeng Lu, Hongkou Qu, Shanghai, China', 'Registered owner, ship and commercial manager of the DONG FENG 6, a vessel that loaded coal at Hamhung, DPRK, on 11 July 2017 for export in violation of UN sanctions.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908696', 'entity', 'SHEN ZHONG INTERNATIONAL SHIPPING', 'SHEN ZHONG INTERNATIONAL SHIPPING', 'DPRK', 'KPe.073', '2018-03-30', NULL, 'Unit 503, 5th Floor, Silvercord Tower 2, 30, Canton Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Kowloon, Hong Kong, China', 'Ship and commercial manager of HAO FAN 2 and HAO FAN 6, St Kitts-Nevis-flagged vessels. The HAO FAN 6 loaded coal at Nampo, DPRK, on 27 August 2017. HAO FAN 2 loaded DPRK coal at Nampo, DPRK, on 3 June 2017.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908697', 'entity', 'WEIHAI WORLD-SHIPPING FREIGHT', 'WEIHAI WORLD SHIPPING FREIGHT', 'DPRK', 'KPe.074', '2018-03-30', NULL, '419-201, Tongyi Lu, Huancui Qu, Weihai, Shandong, China', 'Ship and commercial manager of the XIN GUANG HAI, a vessel that on loaded coal at Taean, DPRK, on 27 October 2017 and had an ETA of 14 November 2017 to Cam Pha, Vietnam, but it did not arrive. IMO number: 5905801.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6908689', 'entity', 'YUK TUNG ENERGY PTE LTD', 'YUK TUNG ENERGY', 'DPRK', 'KPe.075', '2018-03-30', NULL, '80 Raffles Place, #17-22 UOB Plaza, Singapore, Singapore', 'Ship manager and commercial manager of the YUK TUNG, which conducted ship-to-ship transfer of refined petroleum product. IMO number: 5987860.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690782', 'entity', 'LIBYAN INVESTMENT AUTHORITY', 'LIBYAN INVESTMENT AUTHORITY', 'Libya', 'LYe.001', '2011-03-17', NULL, '1 Fateh Tower Office, No 99 22nd Floor, Borgaida Street, Tripoli, Libya', 'Listed pursuant to paragraph 17 of resolution 1973, as modified on 16 September pursuant to paragraph 15 of resolution 2009. INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('690783', 'entity', 'LIBYAN AFRICA INVESTMENT PORTFOLIO', 'LIBYAN AFRICA INVESTMENT PORTFOLIO', 'Libya', 'LYe.002', '2011-03-17', NULL, 'Jamahiriya Street, LAP Building, PO Box 91330, Tripoli, Libya', 'Listed pursuant to paragraph 17 of resolution 1973, as modified on 16 September pursuant to paragraph 15 of resolution 2009. INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('6909645', 'entity', 'AVAX', 'AVAX', 'Libya', 'LYe.006', '2026-07-22', NULL, NULL, 'IMO: 9058713 Listed pursuant to paragraphs 10(a), 10 (b), 10(c) and 10(d) of resolution 2146 (2014), as amended by paragraph 2 of resolutions 2441 (2018) and 2509 (2020) and extended in resolution 2819 (2026) (prohibition to load, transport or discharge; prohibition to enter ports; prohibition to provide bunkering and vessel services; prohibition to engage in financial transactions with regard to petroleum). Pursuant to paragraph 11 of resolution 2146, as modified by paragraph 2 of resolution 2509 (2020), this designation is valid from 22 July 2026 to 22 July 2027, unless terminated earlier by the Committee pursuant to paragraph 12 of resolution 2146 (2014). Flag State: Cameroon. As of 4 April 2026, the vessel was located near the anchorage area of the Benghazi Old Harbour, Libya.', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('113445', 'entity', 'ABU SAYYAF GROUP', 'ABU SAYYAF', 'Al-Qaida', 'QDe.001', '2001-10-06', NULL, 'Philippines', 'Associated with Jemaah Islamiyah (JI) (QDe.092). Current leader is Radulan Sahiron (QDi.208) INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('113457', 'entity', 'AL-ITIHAAD AL-ISLAMIYA / AIAI', 'AL ITIHAAD AL ISLAMIYA AIAI', 'Al-Qaida', 'QDe.002', '2001-10-06', NULL, NULL, 'Reported to have operated in Somalia and Ethiopia and to have merged with Harakat Al-Shabaab Al-Mujaahidiin (Al-Shabaab), which was accepted as an affiliate of Al-Qaida (QDe.004) by Aiman Muhammed Rabi al-Zawahiri (QDi.006) in Feb. 2012, and is also subject to the sanctions measures set out in Security Council resolution 1844 (2008) concerning Somalia and Eritrea (see https://www.un.org/sc/suborg/en/sanctions/751). Leadership included Hassan Dahir Aweys (QDi.042). AIAI has received funds through the Al-Haramain Islamic Foundation (Somalia) (QDe.072) INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('113236', 'entity', 'EGYPTIAN ISLAMIC JIHAD', 'EGYPTIAN ISLAMIC JIHAD', 'Al-Qaida', 'QDe.003', '2001-10-06', NULL, NULL, 'Co-founded by Aiman Muhammed Rabi al-Zawahiri (QDi.006), who was also its military leader INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('113458', 'entity', 'AL-QAIDA', 'AL QAIDA', 'Al-Qaida', 'QDe.004', '2001-10-06', NULL, NULL, 'INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
('113459', 'entity', 'AL RASHID TRUST', 'AL RASHID TRUST', 'Al-Qaida', 'QDe.005', '2001-10-06', NULL, 'Kitas Ghar, Nazimabad 4, Dahgel-Iftah, Karachi, Pakistan; Jamia Maajid, Sulalman Park, Melgium Pura, Lahore, Pakistan; Office Dha’rbi-M’unin, Opposite Khyber Bank, Abbottabad Road, Mansehra, Pakistan; Office Dha’rbi-M’unin ZR Brothers, Katcherry Road, Chowk Yadgaar, Peshawar, Pakistan; Office Dha’rbi-M’unin, Rm No. 3, Moti Plaza, Near Liaquat Bagh, Muree Road, Rawalpindi, Pakistan; Office Dha’rbi-M’unin, Top Floor, Dr. Dawa Khan Dental Clinic Surgeon, Main Baxae, Mingora, Swat, Pakistan; Kitab Ghar, Darul Ifta Wal Irshad, Nazimabad No. 4, Karachi, Pakistan, Phone 6683301; Phone 0300-8209199; Fax 6623814; 302b-40, Good Earth Court, Opposite Pia Planitarium, Block 13a, Gulshan -l Igbal, Karachi, Pakistan; Phone 4979263; 617 Clifton Center, Block 5, 6th Floor, Clifton, Karachi, Pakistan; Phone 587-2545; 605 Landmark Plaza, 11 Chundrigar Road, Opposite Jang Building, Karachi, Pakistan; Phone 2623818-19; Jamia Masjid, Sulaiman Park, Begum Pura, Lahore, Pakistan; Phone 042-6812081', 'Reportedly defunct. Headquarters were in Pakistan. Operations in Afghanistan: Herat Jalalabad, Kabul, Kandahar, Mazar Sherif. Also operations in Kosovo, Chechnya. Involved in the financing of Al-Qaida and the Taliban. Until 21 Oct. 2008, this entity appeared also as "Aid Organization of the Ulema, Pakistan" (QDe.073), listed on 24 Apr. 2002 and amended on 25 Jul. 2006. The two entries Al Rashid Trust (QDe.005) and Aid Organization of the Ulema, Pakistan (QDe.073) were consolidated into this entity on 21 Oct. 2008. Founded by Mufti Rashid Ahmad Ledahyanoy (deceased). Associated with Jaish-i-Mohammed (QDe.019). Banned in Pakistan since Oct. 2001. No indication of any activity under the name of Al-Rashid Trust has emerged as of November 2023 INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities', 'https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/un-sc-consolidated-list', 1, '2026-11-22'),
